$NBIS: Explaining DataOne Winding Down Temporary Generators

In Q3 earnings call, many investors did not understand what was meant by "DataOne decided to wind down the temporary generation faster than it was expected" (1). It's not Nebius or DataOne's fault nor was it permitting issues.  Let me unpack it.

@SMASIMHO was right that Vineland is a 100MW class Fuel Cell site. I thought that it couldn't be the case because 100MW of BTM electric aggregation with voltage and frequency fluctuation smoothing would take longer to build. It turns out we were both right at the same time. …
